call of duty black ops cold war is right  around the corner so let's keep this  hype train moving and discuss  our top 10 kill streaks from the black  ops series kill streaks score streaks  it's all here  let's get into it number 10  rc xd at this point we simply can't have  a black ops game without our favorite  remote controlled companion  the rcxd is a perfect low end kill  streak that's easy  and fun to use perfect for game modes  like domination and search and destroy  the rcxd can clean up a hot spot that's  filled with enemies or  even take out a lone sniper that's been  bugging you from across the map  in black ops 3 our little buddy even got  a hover conversion known as the  hcxd when black ops originally released  in 2010  the special collector's edition came  bundled with a functioning rc xd with a  built-in camera  how cool is that  oh anyway in early 2020 we saw the rc xd  teased in warzone  by the looks of it it was being  assembled with the other half found  later in an unlocked bunker  well after we got our hands on cold  war's multiplayer we're happy to confirm  that this is indeed coming back  so get your battery packs charged and  let's go  can we cut this footage please number  nine  lightning strike task lightning  there's a reason lightning strikes are  in nearly every black ops game  they're a well-rounded low to mid-level  streak that has some  serious potential you pick three  locations to attack  and in and out they go and to be fair  the strike itself is a little too  precise and can miss targets if they  decide to move a few feet  but we all know how it feels when we see  the screen light up with hit markers and  score  on the other hand you're probably not  going to be too upset if you missed the  strike entirely  you'll get another one soon also if  memory serves these came in care  packages quite a bit  number 8 guardian let's talk defense  we're all aware of the numerous sentry  guns that black ops has offered over the  years  they're a defensive staple however most  can be destroyed pretty easily with a  good knifing a well-placed grenade or by  unloading your magazine at a weak spot  here's where guardians have the  advantage while you still have a shot at  landing a grenade or firing off some  shots  the guardian from black ops 2 and 3  microwaves you  from there you have two options keep  firing or get microwaved to death  it's annoying yes but if you need to  hold down a tight spot for a moment the  guardian is your friend stupid bots  hey also depending on the game  automated sentries don't always see  enemies right away  which sucks  number seven sam turret here's another  one for defense  sadly the surface-to-air missile turret  or sam turret  was only featured in black ops one it  was great for support players like me  whose secondary is  always a rocket the sam turret would  fire missiles to take down most airborne  kill streaks  it was one of the best defensive kill  streaks costing only four of your hard  earned kills  on top of that this thing can  accidentally kill other players  observed  nowadays we don't see the sam turret in  most black ops games  so i guess it's back to the rockets for  [Music]  me  number six carpet bomber the almighty  carpet bomber is a menacing and  unforgiving kill streak  it lays waste to anything underneath it  in a slow indestructible  boeing b-52 if he saw this thing in the  air  it was over while other gunships like  the warthog and thresher are similar  the carpet bomber in black ops 3's  bombing run aren't flashy and fast  they're slow and destructive no matter  what game mode you're playing  carpet bombers will destroy everything  in their path  including you number 5  lodestar featured only in black ops 2  the lodestar lets players take control  of the laser-guided missile system  from high in the sky unlike the ac-130s  40 millimeter cannon the lodestar's  missile system is way more forgiving  after it's fired missiles can be guided  to follow targets for improved accuracy  if enemies can manage to whip out their  small rocket in time it'll take  three of them to drop the lodestar out  of the sky  number 4 chopper gunner sometimes in  black ops  less is more this is indeed the case for  the chopper gunner in black ops  one after nine kills players were  rewarded with this show-stopping kill  streak that punished enemies below  controlling a minigun with infinite ammo  and no cooldown you have  60 seconds straight up delete enemies  [Music]  even though a smaller map is preferred i  had no trouble wasting these stupid bots  bots because no one's playing this game  anymore  if you're on xbox and want to get a game  going sometime let me know on twitter  bottom line the chopper gunner is simple  destructive  and awesome number three  stealth chopper sometimes it's nice not  to have to do all the heavy lifting  we've all been there in the middle of  battle you don't want to be interrupted  to control something like a chopper  gunner or a hind  despite how awesome it is you want to be  on the ground in control of your gun  that's where the stealth chopper comes  in this kill streak goes by a few names  including cobra  and wraith but its only goal is to do  the killing for you  since you're not the one in control  stealth choppers can take quite a bit of  extra damage and also come equipped with  flares  so sit back and watch the free kills  pile up  you earned it number 2  the swarm ah yes the elusive final kill  streak from black ops 2.  the wrath of the swarm was an  unforgettable one  if you didn't feel like a champion  calling one in you felt like an absolute  scrub getting repeatedly bombed by it  costing an astounding 1900 points this  mass of hunter killer drones lasted for  45 excruciating  circling above players these hunter  killers are much faster and more  relentless than dogs  so your best chance was to hide indoors  and take cover  be advised swarm inbound number one  attack dogs beginning before the black  ops series  treyarch introduced attack dogs in  2008's call of duty world at war  since then they've been used in one form  or another across all four black ops  games  cementing them as a powerful high-level  kill streak you call them in and they  relentlessly attack enemies for 60  seconds  personally i dig the robotic  anti-personnel sentries aka the raps  from black ops 3  all the danger of dogs without actually  harming them  listen they even growl  oh if you want to share your favorite  killstreak memories or have an idea for  another call of duty video  find me down in the comments thanks for  watching  [Music]  you
 

